---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import PageIntro from "../components/PageIntro.astro";
import { SITE } from "../consts";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Contributing"
  description="Contribute to the Kwechiri compiler, documentation, tests, and educational material."
>
  <PageIntro
    eyebrow="Community"
    title="Make changes that preserve the contract."
    lead="Kwechiri welcomes focused engineering, documentation, testing, and educational work that respects the approved language scope."
  />

  <section class="section">
    <div class="shell prose">
      <h2>Before changing code</h2>
      <ol>
        <li>Read the repository's AGENTS.md and current project status.</li>
        <li>Inspect the applicable specification, architecture, and ADRs.</li>
        <li>Confirm that the requested milestone or stabilization scope is approved.</li>
        <li>Inspect existing work and preserve unrelated changes.</li>
      </ol>

      <h2>Validation</h2>
      <pre tabindex="0"><code>npm ci
npm run check
npm ci --prefix website
npm run website:check</code></pre>
      <p>
        A successful build alone is not enough for user-visible behavior. Add
        direct CLI, runtime, module, or browser probes when the risk calls for
        them.
      </p>

      <h2>Language changes require approval</h2>
      <p>
        New syntax, keywords, semantics, public APIs, compatibility changes, and
        major architecture decisions require the project owner's approval and
        the appropriate specification or ADR.
      </p>

      <div class="callout callout--green">
        <strong>Start with the repository</strong>
        <a href={SITE.github}>Visit the Kwechiri project on GitHub</a> to inspect
        issues, source, tests, and developer documentation.
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
